Data Science Career Goals:
One career goal I have is determining which subset of data science I want to go into. Data science is a very versatile field, and it is used in most fields. I am currently leading towards economics or psychology, but I need to make a decision and do research to determine which one I would like to pursue.

If I choose economics, I would like to work in a company to help make financial decisions using previous experiences to predict what will happen next. 

If I choose psychology, I would like to study human behaviors and use statistical analysis to make informed predictions and apply these to the real world. 

Regardless of what I do, I want to use statistical analysis to make informed decisions to help people’s lives. I will gather, analyze, and interpret data to do this. Afterwards, I will communicate my findings to a team so that they can take action on my findings.

To achieve these goals, I will hone my teamwork skills. Regardless of which option I choose, teamwork is an essential skill. This not only connects to when I have my job, but also to getting my job. Having good teamwork skills will allow me to network, meet new people, and further develop my career. Through the use of teamwork, I will use statistical analysis to better people's lives from either an economic or psychological standpoint.
